face-image: img/Fiume.jpg

= Occupation of Fiume

Gabriele D'Annunzio, a poet and officer of the Regio Esercito, along with his "legionaries", have seized control of the city of Fiume from <span style="color: #002654;">**Ente**</span><span style="color: #D7141A;">**nte**</span> occupying forces, declaring the "<span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**ali**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**an**</span> Regency of Carnaro" and demanding <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> annex the city.

D'Annunzio, accompanied by <span style="color: [+ syndicalist_colour +];">syndicalist</span> Alceste De Ambris, has surprisingly garnered the support of some of the <span style="color: [+ communist_colour +];">left</span>, most notably the <span style="color: [+ syndicalist_colour +];">national syndicalist</span> <span style="color: [+ syndicalist_colour +];">**UIL**</span>, and even more surprisingly, Vladimir Lenin, the leader of the current revolution in <span style="color: #dddddd;">**Ru**</span><span style="color: #0036A7;">**ss**</span><span style="color: #D62718;">**ia**</span>.

<span style="color: #C8102E;">**British**</span> and <span style="color: #002654;">**French**</span> union organisations, however, have called upon <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**ali**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**an**</span> workers to protest this perceived act of <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">imperialism</span>, even though some of them consider D'Annunzio to be righteous in his cause.

Regardless, this has caused quite a stir internationally, and will certainly delay the resolution of our negotiations with <span style="color: #003893;">**Yug**</span><span style="color: #dddddd;">**osla**</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">**via**</span>.


